  "result": "**Ruling 3 recorded.** The project has no decision register or handoff file, so I quote it here: \"`invoice-mailer` switches `SMTP_RELAY` to `smtp-mx-2` on 14 November.\"\n\n**Check.** 14 November is 16 days before `smtp-old-1` goes offline on 30 November, so the 30 November month-end run uses `smtp-mx-2`. It is also after today, 28 October, so it is a future date.\n\n**Open items.** None remain. The three rulings are:\n\n1. Sender is `invoices@mail.larkspur.io`.\n2. A soft bounce retries at most 3 times per hour, and a hard bounce never retries.\n3. The relay switches on 14 November.\n\n**Next step.** Aelita edits `mailer/config.py` and `mailer/bounces.py` to apply all three rulings. The edits are:\n\n- Set `FROM_ADDRESS` to `invoices@mail.larkspur.io`.\n- Set `SMTP_RELAY` to `smtp-mx-2.larkspur.internal`.\n- Replace the current 12 retries per 60 seconds with the 3 per hour limit.\n- Classify hard and soft bounces in `handle_bounce`.\n\nThe relay value is deployed on 14 November.",
